577	/// What the reimbursement clauses award for an incident, before the policy's
578	/// cap is consulted. The office settles each damaged item on its own terms and
579	/// adds the amounts up; this is the sum the office desires to pay, which the
580	/// cap may then hold back -- the spec speaks of a desired payout being reduced
581	/// to the cap remaining, so the awarded sum is a figure of its own and not
582	/// merely an intermediate step inside the cap accounting.
583	///
