693	/// office insures the types its price list names and no others, so an item it
694	/// does not recognise is refused rather than priced -- a quote that lists a
695	/// broomstick yields no premium. The office names the offending type in its
696	/// refusal; which types it admits is the price list's own knowledge, read
697	/// here rather than restated.
698	fn admit_the_listed_items(items: &[Item]) -> Result<(), String> {
