709	/// has on file about the customer.
710	///
711	/// A refusal is carried as the office's own description of what it objects to.
712	/// The office refuses documents for several unrelated reasons -- an unlisted
713	/// item type here, a damage outside the policy on the claim side -- but no
714	/// caller distinguishes them: the specification asks only that a refusal reach
715	/// stderr and the exit status be non-zero, so every reason is rendered the same
716	/// way. A named error type would be built at each refusal and flattened back to
